WEBVTT

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.790
You can float on forever.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.750
However...

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.580
I want to fly under my own power.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.210
I don't even care if I fall...

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.630
so long as it's in a real sky.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:40.490
There was once a war with a race of giants known as the Zentradi.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.250
After first contact with an extraterrestrial entity led to war,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:52.340
Humanity, having faced the possibility of extinction, entrusted its future to the colonization of outer space,

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.800
and set sail for new lands all across the galaxy.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.850
2059 A.D.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.480
The 25th massive colonial fleet to be created,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.690
Macross Frontier,

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:17.320
is continuing its expedition toward the center of the galaxy.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.160
At the same time,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.120
a lone songstress descends towards this frontier,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.130
having crossed the sea of stars.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.880
You are approaching the area of artificial gravity.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.890
Please watch your step.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.400
What an extremely lively city.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.270
That said, are you prepared for this?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.490
In case you can't find your "target," what will you do?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.910
Grace... I'm Sheryl.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:08.200
Sheryl Nome always sings at her best.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.380
You're kidding! You really got tickets to Sheryl's concert?!

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.460
Well, yeah.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:24.260
That's because Michael, Luca, and I will be doing the aerobatics at the performance.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.270
I'll pass one on to you.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.600
Thank you, Alto-kun!

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.610
There are a lot of take-out orders today, so wait for me, okay?

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.360
Oh, Deculture!

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.870
I'm really going to see it!

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.670
I'm heading out!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.190
How's it going, Luca?

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.400
The maneuvers for later, that is.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.360
Start with a Split S,

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.570
then go from a triple loop to a sudden bank and ascent.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.740
We'll go with this for now.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.280
What nonsense.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.290
I couldn't care less about it.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.880
Is this about the harsh treatment you received
during our rehearsal with the Galactic Fairy?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.960
I just always want to fly to extent of my abilities, that's all.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.090
Then if you end up accidentally crashing into the crowd,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.970
just who will take responsibility for it?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.090
I won't make any mistakes.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:33.470
Oh, such open-mindedness, but don't you have
any regrets, leaving the kabuki stage?

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.600
Genius "actress," Princess Alto.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.480
What did you just say!?

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.820
You make such a fabulous face when you're angry.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.820
What was that?!

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.070
Here we go again.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.030
Honestly...

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.690
My dear princess...

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.700
Klan-senpai!

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:45.700
What!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:46.780
Buzz off!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.360
They're no different from a bunch of kids.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.570
One more time and—

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.030
Thank you for waiting! This is Nyan Nyan!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.120
If you could only see the look on your face—

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.080
Why you—

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:52.990
You think I'll forgive you?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.450
Ranka!

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.460
Oh, Ranka-chan! That was fast.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.040
Yeah.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.880
Well then everyone, here's Nyan Nyan's marvelous "Galactic Ramen."

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.260
Today you also get the "Magellanic Cloud" for free as a bonus!

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.640
Wow, magellanic naruto! Let's eat!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.810
The smell of this soup is quite charming.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:14.890
Let's eat!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.440
Hey, come back! Wait a minute, Klan!

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.400
I just couldn't help it!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.190
Hey, Alto-kun.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:28.610
Do you want to eat together?

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.950
We can have Nyan Nyan's deluxe tuna buns!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.410
No, thank you. I need to keep my weight down for flying.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:39.620
Th-These are...

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.270
It's here!

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.650
Go!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.660
North-northwesterly wind.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.910
Four meters per second.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.410
Ranka-chan?

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.670
Connected to the catapult.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.880
Five,

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:29.970
four,

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:30.880
three,

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.130
two,

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.260
one,

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:33.930
Go!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.350
Take off!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:49.820
All right!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.830
In the beginning was the song.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:07.170
Stars sing as if they're playing a beautiful tune of heaven.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.050
Lynn Minmay 2009

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.970
Sharon Apple 2040

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.930
Fire Bomber 2045

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.560
It's starting.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:20.850
And now...

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.480
Listen to my song!

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:36.820
Target confirmed.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.320
Stabilizers released.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.990
Nina... Johnny...

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.630
Amazing!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.800
The Galactic Fairy...

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.020
Bravo 1 and 3 have been destroyed.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.390
Golf 7 damaged, returning to base.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.690
The second attack wave of unmanned vehicles is cleared to engage the unknowns.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.110
Intercept in 10 seconds.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:05.820
8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2...

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:08.790
Electro-magnetic bursts?!

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:21.590
Is it true? The unknowns are interfering with the control systems of the missiles and Ghosts?

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.260
Y-Yes, Mr. President.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.270
Don't screw this up!

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.850
She must be kidding me!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.620
What was that for?

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.170
We're going to keep going!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:40.840
Seriously...

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.010
That idiot!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.220
All backup fliers, follow his lead.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:33.140
This is S.M.S. Skull Squadron leader,
Ozma Lee, to New U.N. space fighter.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.060
We're taking control of this area.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.270
R-Roger that!

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.310
These aren't opponents you cowards could fight.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.280
Code Victor, so this is what you were talking about, Captain.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.240
Let's go!

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.440
What are these things?

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.280
Go defend the city, Gilliam!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.820
You don't have to tell me!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.580
Seriously, what were you thinking?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:38.620
Don't you get it? It's entertainment. Entertainment.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.210
Stop messing with me!
If I'd been even a little bit slower, then...

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.460
And it wouldn't have been just you, but the audience too!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.050
Living unpredictably makes life interesting, doesn't it?

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:52.510
I just wanted to do something more thrilling than mere singing.

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:53.640
What was that?!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:57.100
Aren't you the one who said
"Don't look down on us!" during the rehearsals?

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:02.100
I was only evaluating just how well you could fly.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.610
A gas jet cluster?!

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:14.450
You're such an idiot. Only an amateur would do that without something to fall back on.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.490
Come on, the next number is about to start!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:18.290
Hey!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:25.250
An evacuation order has been issued. An evacuation order has been issued.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:29.670
All citizens, please report to the nearest shelter.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.420
This is not a drill.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.180
No way!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.260
Roger, we'll return immediately.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.760
Let's go, Luca.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.510
Understood.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:42.230
Evacuate?! My live performance has only just begun!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.980
Damn it, what the hell is going on out there?

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.570
Purple and Vermilion Squadrons: annihilated.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.780
The final line of defense has been breached!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.410
They're boarding Island 1!

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:06.170
Expand the repulsion field!
Use all the available energy we've got!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.470
What's going on here?

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:25.190
It's dangerous here, you idiot. Hurry and get to a shelter.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:29.110
No, I won't! I don't want my
precious concert to end on such a bad note!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.570
I can't just leave without saying a word!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.240
No way!

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:48.830
This is dangerous!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:52.920
Sheryl!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.310
Calm down, calm down, calm down!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:08.690
Sheryl! Fly!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:09.980
But...

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.190
Use the jets around your waist!

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.800
What's going on here?

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:58.610
Hold on tight!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:18:59.910
Okay.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.130
A VF-25?

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.090
It's already been deployed to combat status?

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.720
Damn monsters!

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:28.330
I won't die in here!

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:33.250
You monster!

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:43.970
Stop it!

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:56.860
Ranka!

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:09.700
Stay put!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:14.870
Don't come...

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:28.430
I can do this.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:59.130
That's not Gilliam.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.130
Who is it?

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:03.510
Ranka!

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:05.760
Why is she <i>here</i> of all places?

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:12.760
Out of ammo?

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:14.470
This is bad!

00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:26.490
Please... stop.

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:34.040
An Armored?

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:37.250
Who are you? What happened to Gilliam?

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:38.960
I...

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:42.000
More importantly, what's with these monsters?

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:43.590
What's going on?!

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:03.900
Amazing.

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:13.780
Are you all right, Ranka?

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:16.370
Get a hold of yourself, Ranka!

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.830
It's me, Ranka!

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.590
Onii-chan.

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.050
Onii-chan, you say?

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:30.470
Good, get up! We need to get out of here quickly.

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:42.230
No!

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:45.650
Onii-chan! Onii-chan, Onii-chan!

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:53.910
Why... why would you do such a thing?

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:58.160
I... never wanted anything like this to happen.

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:09.510
No!

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:14.590
What is this fold response?

00:24:38.330 --> 00:24:39.080
Alto?

00:24:54.630 --> 00:24:55.680
It's over.

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:04.560
I've come to escort you back, Sheryl-sama.

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:11.650
My apologies, I never expected
the Vajra invasion force to arrive so quickly.

00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:14.650
Brera! How did you arrive so fortuitously?!

00:25:18.580 --> 00:25:21.700
Right shoulder and left foot injured, a total of seven bruises.

00:25:22.120 --> 00:25:24.750
There also seems to be some bleeding on the right wrist.

00:25:24.750 --> 00:25:25.870
In general, however, they are all slight injuries.

00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:29.380
Stop it! Haven't I told you to never scan my body!

00:25:29.630 --> 00:25:30.920
How could you forget that?

00:25:33.510 --> 00:25:37.760
Ms. Grace is waiting for us. We must return before we get involved in more trouble.

00:25:37.970 --> 00:25:38.550
If you don't mind...

00:25:41.930 --> 00:25:43.220
W-Wait, not yet!

00:25:44.270 --> 00:25:47.650
We'll be taking the shortest route back, please hold on tight.

00:25:48.770 --> 00:25:49.560
Brera!

00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:28.270
So they're finally going after our fleet now.

00:26:29.310 --> 00:26:32.820
Here are the casualty and damage reports.

00:26:33.070 --> 00:26:37.740
Also, here are the propaganda plans for the mass media and the net.

00:26:38.780 --> 00:26:41.660
You're on top of things as always.

00:26:43.330 --> 00:26:45.330
It is an honor to receive your praise.

00:26:49.040 --> 00:26:52.670
Don't you think the timing is a bit too convenient though?

00:26:53.460 --> 00:26:57.760
Are you saying that Sheryl Nome's visit is part of the Galaxy fleet's strategy?

00:26:58.470 --> 00:27:02.470
This isn't just about investigating the Vajra.
Continue to broaden the scope of the investigation.

00:27:48.390 --> 00:27:50.020
Unpredictable, huh?

00:28:02.160 --> 00:28:03.950
It can't be... back then...

00:28:05.240 --> 00:28:09.870
After a series of attacks on the fleet, the government held a combined funeral for the victims of the tragedy.

00:28:10.540 --> 00:28:16.090
According to the Army Chief of Staff at NUNS Headquarters, 228 people are listed as casualties of the battle.

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:23.130
During the funeral, President Glass expressed his condolences and promised the bereaved families adequate compensation.

00:28:23.930 --> 00:28:25.800
A private military company?

00:28:26.010 --> 00:28:26.640
That's right.

00:28:27.390 --> 00:28:32.560
Michael, Luca, and I are part of the S.M.S., not the army.

00:28:32.850 --> 00:28:33.520
Captain Ozma!

00:28:33.690 --> 00:28:34.650
I know.

00:28:35.230 --> 00:28:38.270
To begin with, this is a somewhat unusual situation.

00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:43.110
We are tasked with evaluating the state-of-the-art VF-25 before it is approved for procurement by the army.

00:28:44.030 --> 00:28:45.410
But back then...

00:28:45.410 --> 00:28:46.120
Right.

00:28:46.660 --> 00:28:51.200
We, the SMS, can act independently as a civilian organization.

00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:56.750
Therefore, it is up to you, Saotome Alto, to decide whether or not you want to become one of us.

00:28:57.790 --> 00:28:59.380
So you're blackmailing me.

00:29:00.130 --> 00:29:03.970
My sister, Ranka; I am grateful that you saved her.

00:29:04.720 --> 00:29:07.390
Ranka? Is Ranka okay?

00:29:08.260 --> 00:29:12.810
The truth is that Ranka is traumatized by the
thought of losing people who are close to her

00:29:12.810 --> 00:29:14.850
because of an event in her past.

00:29:15.190 --> 00:29:18.980
Dissociative Amnesia.

00:29:21.110 --> 00:29:24.030
Due to a traumatic or stressful event,

00:29:24.030 --> 00:29:26.740
it becomes impossible to recall certain memories.

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:29.830
However, certain things can trigger these residual memories,

00:29:29.830 --> 00:29:32.200
leading to recollections of intense unhappiness or fear.

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:34.960
In other words, she has a problem with her memory.

00:29:35.870 --> 00:29:37.580
Ranka has already recovered.

00:29:37.790 --> 00:29:39.880
I hope you don't mind, I've discharged her already.

00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:42.630
You've always been so helpful, Canaria.

00:29:42.670 --> 00:29:43.760
Don't worry about it.

00:29:45.130 --> 00:29:46.880
A certain event, you said?

00:29:47.550 --> 00:29:50.890
Ranka lost her entire family long ago.

00:29:51.640 --> 00:29:54.020
Parents, siblings, all of them.

00:29:55.230 --> 00:29:56.730
But aren't you...

00:29:57.310 --> 00:29:59.520
I'm not Ranka's real older brother.

00:30:00.480 --> 00:30:05.780
I'm just a worthless pilot who couldn't protect her family 11 years ago.

00:30:06.530 --> 00:30:08.530
Ranka has already forgotten all that,

00:30:09.660 --> 00:30:11.870
along with everything else about that horrible incident.

00:30:12.330 --> 00:30:15.370
Horrible incident? What are you talking about?

00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:19.330
Once you've heard it, you can't turn back.

00:30:20.630 --> 00:30:24.010
I don't care, I want to know everything.

00:30:27.010 --> 00:30:29.010
I'll give you 24 hours to consider it.

00:30:29.340 --> 00:30:30.720
Think about it one more time.

00:30:31.720 --> 00:30:33.350
"What do I want to do?"

00:30:33.640 --> 00:30:36.680
"What are my reasons?" "What am I fighting for?"

00:30:40.310 --> 00:30:43.230
Are you going to run away again, Alto?

00:30:44.150 --> 00:30:46.280
Run away? Who's going to?

00:30:46.690 --> 00:30:51.200
A real war is very different from the stage performances you're used to.

00:30:51.240 --> 00:30:53.160
Obviously, I'm aware of that!

00:30:53.160 --> 00:30:54.620
No, you don't understand.

00:30:55.910 --> 00:31:00.670
The way things are now, you might get yourself or someone else killed.

00:31:16.470 --> 00:31:18.390
He was a gallant soldier.

00:31:18.940 --> 00:31:20.480
Fearless and unflinching,

00:31:20.560 --> 00:31:25.360
he fought with all his strength and
sacrificed his life for countless others.

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:28.490
However, this is not the end.

00:31:29.110 --> 00:31:33.450
His flesh shall become our flesh, our blood,

00:31:33.450 --> 00:31:36.200
the air from which our own lives spring forth.

00:31:37.790 --> 00:31:40.500
So, rest now, my comrade.

00:31:41.250 --> 00:31:43.670
Farewell, until we meet again!

00:31:45.710 --> 00:31:46.460
Salute!

00:31:57.850 --> 00:32:00.730
<i>Are you going to run away again, Alto?</i>

00:32:01.730 --> 00:32:03.060
<i>This isn't a stage performance...</i>

00:32:04.360 --> 00:32:05.310
This is different!

00:32:05.940 --> 00:32:08.990
I'm... I'm...!

00:32:33.470 --> 00:32:34.050
Ranka?

00:32:35.390 --> 00:32:36.600
Alto-kun!

00:32:40.520 --> 00:32:41.730
That's a nice song.

00:32:42.730 --> 00:32:46.860
I don't remember anything from my childhood.

00:32:48.230 --> 00:32:50.610
But I do remember this song.

00:32:51.740 --> 00:32:54.160
It's my one and only memory.

00:32:56.410 --> 00:32:57.200
I see.

00:32:58.240 --> 00:33:01.580
You know... sometimes I come to this hill to sing it.

00:33:02.370 --> 00:33:04.670
Because no one can hear it here.

00:33:09.630 --> 00:33:14.340
I've always taken living for granted.

00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:18.930
I wake up in the morning,
wash my face, eat a delicious breakfast...

00:33:19.680 --> 00:33:23.980
quarrel or have fun with my brother or you guys.

00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:30.730
However, it isn't that simple, is it? People, the world...

00:33:32.030 --> 00:33:34.070
Geez, are you even listening, Alto-kun?!

00:33:36.070 --> 00:33:37.200
Isn't it incredible?

00:33:38.240 --> 00:33:43.540
That even a simple piece of paper, folded a few times,

00:33:44.040 --> 00:33:46.210
becomes a plane that can fly through the sky.

00:33:47.580 --> 00:33:49.000
You really like those things, don't you?

00:33:50.380 --> 00:33:53.300
A paper plane is kinda like an actor!

00:33:54.090 --> 00:33:57.550
An ordinary piece of paper that changes form into something that flies through the skies!

00:33:58.340 --> 00:34:00.470
I have no interest in becoming an actor again, okay?

00:34:04.100 --> 00:34:06.640
I wonder if I could fly too.

00:34:07.560 --> 00:34:08.730
It's impossible.

00:34:12.230 --> 00:34:14.690
I guess it is... for someone like me.

00:34:15.700 --> 00:34:20.950
As long as you keep saying "If I could—" and "someone like me—" then yeah...

00:34:22.120 --> 00:34:23.120
You'll never do it!

00:34:32.630 --> 00:34:34.340
You're so mean, Alto-kun!

00:34:34.920 --> 00:34:35.760
I guess.

00:34:36.260 --> 00:34:38.260
I want to share it with everyone!

00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:40.090
So please listen to it.

00:34:40.090 --> 00:34:41.100
My song.

00:34:41.640 --> 00:34:42.970
Do whatever you want.

00:34:43.720 --> 00:34:45.310
Thank you, Alto-kun!

00:35:22.300 --> 00:35:24.600
That's right, I want to fly as well.

00:35:25.680 --> 00:35:29.020
Even if I have to fight in those skies.

00:35:44.910 --> 00:35:45.950
That voice...

00:35:57.630 --> 00:35:58.510
It can't be!

00:35:59.050 --> 00:35:59.970
It's you.

00:36:01.550 --> 00:36:03.970
This kind of service isn't something I do very often.

00:36:05.680 --> 00:36:06.680
Sheryl-san.

00:36:08.270 --> 00:36:09.520
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:36:10.180 --> 00:36:13.560
You have a nice voice. What's your name?

00:36:14.900 --> 00:36:17.020
I'm Ranka, Ranka Lee.

00:36:17.320 --> 00:36:18.480
What nice voice?

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:21.700
There's no need to be so humble.

00:36:22.070 --> 00:36:22.950
However...

00:36:23.660 --> 00:36:24.530
However?

00:36:24.660 --> 00:36:27.540
How is it that you know the song "Aimo"?

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:30.790
"Aimo"?

00:36:36.340 --> 00:36:38.170
That's right, "Aimo."

00:36:43.470 --> 00:36:45.890
What the... now the mood is ruined!

00:36:46.850 --> 00:36:48.010
Hello, Grace.

00:36:50.220 --> 00:36:52.230
No way, it's already time for my film shoot?

00:36:52.940 --> 00:36:54.810
A slight delay shouldn't matter at all.

00:36:55.900 --> 00:36:59.480
Live broadcast? I understand.
I'll be there as soon as possible, okay?

00:37:00.780 --> 00:37:01.990
Sorry!

00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:04.450
It's already show time.

00:37:04.610 --> 00:37:07.370
I'll be going then. Let's continue talking some other time, okay?

00:37:08.780 --> 00:37:10.540
What's up with her?

00:37:11.080 --> 00:37:13.500
How does she know that song?

00:37:21.550 --> 00:37:26.010
Alto Saotome, 2nd year in
Mihoshi Academy's pilot development course.

00:37:27.050 --> 00:37:30.600
As of today, I will formally become a member of the S.M.S. regiment.

00:37:31.680 --> 00:37:32.980
I'll ask you one more time.

00:37:33.230 --> 00:37:37.610
There are unknown hazards waiting for you any time you go into space.

00:37:38.150 --> 00:37:39.360
Are you prepared for that?

00:37:39.940 --> 00:37:40.980
Of course!

00:37:41.030 --> 00:37:43.740
I mean... I am aware and fully prepared, Major Ozma.

00:37:44.070 --> 00:37:47.620
He's so dreamy... as expected of a
kabuki actor who plays women's roles.

00:37:48.410 --> 00:37:49.910
He seems energetic!

00:37:49.910 --> 00:37:51.620
How delicious!

00:37:52.700 --> 00:37:57.290
Very well, from now on we will consider you a member of S.M.S., welcome!

00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:03.840
Damn it!

00:38:07.260 --> 00:38:10.100
S.M.S. new recruit initiation rite!

00:38:14.890 --> 00:38:15.850
Why you...

00:38:16.690 --> 00:38:18.150
Enlisted

00:38:21.570 --> 00:38:22.980
Are those guys for real?

00:38:23.320 --> 00:38:25.610
What's up with that new recruit initiation rite?

00:38:25.610 --> 00:38:28.410
They just screwed around until morning.

00:38:34.830 --> 00:38:37.040
What's that for all of a sudden?!

00:38:37.040 --> 00:38:37.870
Hi!

00:38:43.090 --> 00:38:45.880
Are you sure it's okay for you to
just go off on your own like this?

00:38:46.380 --> 00:38:48.550
Aren't you too famous for that?

00:38:48.550 --> 00:38:50.800
Oh, so you don't want to come with me?

00:38:50.850 --> 00:38:52.720
Yeah, it's bothersome.

00:38:52.720 --> 00:38:57.890
But I have to return to Galaxy next week, so today is my only chance.

00:38:59.600 --> 00:39:01.110
I <i>have</i> to find it.

00:39:02.190 --> 00:39:03.940
That gem conveys my feelings.

00:39:05.230 --> 00:39:07.150
It's my precious protective charm.

00:39:07.700 --> 00:39:09.070
Conveys your feelings?

00:39:10.360 --> 00:39:13.490
If it's not here, then it might be in the cockpit.

00:39:15.410 --> 00:39:17.330
What do you think you're doing,

00:39:17.660 --> 00:39:20.880
joining the Miss Macross contest without consulting me?

00:39:20.880 --> 00:39:23.040
Look, you even got suspended from school!

00:39:23.670 --> 00:39:27.880
Do you know how hard I worked to get you into that girl's private school?

00:39:28.260 --> 00:39:30.010
It's not like I asked for it.

00:39:30.010 --> 00:39:32.140
I just want to be a singer!

00:39:32.390 --> 00:39:34.100
You should quit your wishful thinking!

00:39:34.220 --> 00:39:36.930
Someone as shy as you could never become a singer!

00:39:39.350 --> 00:39:41.810
You idiot, Onii-chan!

00:39:42.060 --> 00:39:43.610
Idiot! Idiot! Idiot!

00:39:44.230 --> 00:39:45.360
Idiot!

00:39:46.400 --> 00:39:49.450
It's no use, it seems the person in charge is off duty today.

00:39:49.450 --> 00:39:51.570
I thought you said "leave it to me"!

00:39:51.570 --> 00:39:56.200
Hand it over, let me talk to the official in charge of lost property and possessions.

00:39:55.490 --> 00:39:56.580
I said stop it!

00:39:56.700 --> 00:39:59.000
I'll be back at work tomorrow, so I'll search for it then!

00:39:59.250 --> 00:40:03.040
Very well... then I guess I'll be keeping this as collateral.

00:40:05.630 --> 00:40:06.460
Give that back!

00:40:07.920 --> 00:40:08.960
Come and get it.

00:40:09.340 --> 00:40:10.470
That's not fair!

00:40:12.930 --> 00:40:15.350
Listen, Michael, this is an order from your captain:

00:40:15.390 --> 00:40:17.220
Be sure to find Ranka and bring her back!

00:40:17.260 --> 00:40:20.430
Wh-Why would you suddenly—

00:40:22.140 --> 00:40:24.270
Has something happened to Ranka?

00:40:24.400 --> 00:40:25.230
Sort of.

00:40:26.520 --> 00:40:28.480
You're always like that.

00:40:28.480 --> 00:40:31.740
Maybe if you had been that concerned about me—

00:40:33.240 --> 00:40:34.870
That's all over now.

00:40:35.740 --> 00:40:36.620
You're right.

00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:39.120
It's all in the past now.

00:40:40.200 --> 00:40:42.250
No, it's not Ranka.

00:40:42.330 --> 00:40:43.370
Then who is it?

00:40:44.040 --> 00:40:47.210
Luca told me that you were walking around with a girl.

00:40:47.880 --> 00:40:49.340
It doesn't matter who it is.

00:40:51.720 --> 00:40:57.100
Anyway, our Captain with the sister complex
told me that Ranka got suspended from school.

00:40:57.510 --> 00:41:00.600
Suspended? Geez, what did she do?

00:41:01.100 --> 00:41:02.810
I understand, if I see her—

00:41:04.270 --> 00:41:05.310
What are you doing?!

00:41:05.560 --> 00:41:07.270
Making excuses to your girlfriend?

00:41:07.690 --> 00:41:08.320
Huh?

00:41:08.730 --> 00:41:11.440
You're going out with the girl who sang on the hill, aren't you?

00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:14.450
Going out— It's not like that!

00:41:15.450 --> 00:41:16.410
So you aren't?

00:41:17.530 --> 00:41:21.910
Anyway, how did you know that song from Ranka's memories?

00:41:22.830 --> 00:41:25.750
So you really are concerned about Ranka-chan.

00:41:25.960 --> 00:41:27.290
That's not it!

00:41:29.840 --> 00:41:34.340
If you want to find out more about that song, then try to catch me!

00:41:35.470 --> 00:41:36.260
Hey!

00:41:47.060 --> 00:41:49.610
What are you looking around like that for?

00:41:49.900 --> 00:41:52.280
You really are popular, aren't you?

00:41:57.030 --> 00:41:59.370
How do you know I have your earring?

00:42:00.030 --> 00:42:04.080
Grace, my manager, recorded her vision.

00:42:04.080 --> 00:42:04.750
Vision?

00:42:05.080 --> 00:42:06.040
She has implants.

00:42:06.460 --> 00:42:09.840
Are those the things that they stick in your brain?

00:42:10.340 --> 00:42:11.460
But aren't they illegal?

00:42:11.500 --> 00:42:13.960
Oh? They're quite common on Galaxy.

00:42:14.800 --> 00:42:16.470
Since when did they become that popular?

00:42:17.930 --> 00:42:21.220
Have you ever been to Galaxy before?

00:42:21.220 --> 00:42:23.720
Yeah... I was there once as a child.

00:42:23.720 --> 00:42:24.640
I thought so.

00:42:26.100 --> 00:42:27.810
It's different now compared to back then.

00:42:27.810 --> 00:42:30.610
Whether you've had plastic surgery or whether you're a cyborg doesn't matter anymore.

00:42:32.780 --> 00:42:34.030
Then, are you—

00:42:34.030 --> 00:42:35.610
No, not me.

00:42:35.940 --> 00:42:38.030
I'm completely natural.

00:42:38.450 --> 00:42:40.160
It's one of my selling points.

00:42:59.510 --> 00:43:00.510
No means <i>no</i>!

00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:03.510
I definitely won't go back until my brother accepts my decision.

00:43:03.850 --> 00:43:07.350
But the captain— your brother is very worried.

00:43:08.100 --> 00:43:08.890
Where are you going?

00:43:11.270 --> 00:43:12.650
Anywhere is fine!

00:43:13.520 --> 00:43:15.400
This is why I hate dealing with kids.

00:43:16.280 --> 00:43:20.610
But I can't just let her run away now that I've finally found her.

00:43:22.660 --> 00:43:24.280
Wait up, Ranka!

00:43:46.810 --> 00:43:48.180
This feels great!

00:43:48.430 --> 00:43:50.190
If you keep going like that you might—

00:43:50.190 --> 00:43:53.480
Oh? If you're going to catch me, you'd better start trying!

00:43:55.480 --> 00:43:56.650
Then here I come!

00:43:59.240 --> 00:44:00.570
Hurry, hurry!

00:44:00.570 --> 00:44:02.030
All right, the woods are coming up!

00:44:05.240 --> 00:44:06.290
Faster!

00:44:42.780 --> 00:44:46.370
I never knew the birds sang this deep in the forest.

00:44:48.370 --> 00:44:49.830
This area is simply astounding, isn't it?

00:44:52.120 --> 00:44:53.250
Astounding area you say?

00:44:54.080 --> 00:44:58.340
I think that someone like you causing havoc in the forest is even more astounding.

00:45:18.980 --> 00:45:19.610
Sheryl!

00:45:30.910 --> 00:45:32.000
Just what are you doing.

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:33.710
That's supposed to be my line, you idiot!

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:33.000
You pervert!

00:45:33.710 --> 00:45:35.000
Look around!

00:45:40.750 --> 00:45:42.210
Oh, that's right.

00:45:42.920 --> 00:45:45.260
You just saved me again.

00:45:46.970 --> 00:45:47.640
Geez...

00:45:53.390 --> 00:45:54.560
What are you doing?

00:45:54.560 --> 00:45:55.350
Don't move.

00:46:00.690 --> 00:46:03.740
There aren't a lot of organic things aboard the ship you're from, right?

00:46:04.650 --> 00:46:07.240
You might not have an immunity to diseases yet.

00:46:07.910 --> 00:46:09.200
That's why this is a precaution.

00:46:12.290 --> 00:46:13.950
That's very thoughtful of you.

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:18.210
It's... something I learned from training recently.

00:46:18.630 --> 00:46:20.840
I see, are you a soldier?

00:46:22.630 --> 00:46:23.960
I hate the army...

00:46:24.510 --> 00:46:27.050
having to follow someone's orders even if they go against your nature.

00:46:28.430 --> 00:46:31.100
So you're part of some private military company?

00:46:32.010 --> 00:46:33.140
You know about them?

00:46:33.390 --> 00:46:34.390
A little.

00:46:34.810 --> 00:46:38.440
So you'll put yourself in danger as long as you get paid for it?

00:46:38.440 --> 00:46:40.230
I'm not really in it for the money.

00:46:41.570 --> 00:46:44.440
Oh come on, you can be honest. We're both professionals.

00:46:44.820 --> 00:46:45.490
Professionals?

00:46:46.190 --> 00:46:49.870
I'm a professional singer, and you're a professional soldier.

00:46:53.790 --> 00:46:57.120
If you're going to put it that way, I'd prefer you call me a professional pilot instead.

00:47:02.460 --> 00:47:03.750
The sky, huh?

00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:07.760
I hope that someday I'll be able to go to a planet with an atmosphere

00:47:07.760 --> 00:47:09.260
and fly in a real sky.

00:47:10.970 --> 00:47:16.220
An atmosphere... I'm sure there'll be of a lot of different scents in it.

00:47:18.560 --> 00:47:19.850
So it really is true.

00:47:20.810 --> 00:47:23.900
You really don't have implants. You're just a natural human being.

00:47:24.440 --> 00:47:25.070
Idiot!

00:47:43.500 --> 00:47:44.250
This song!

00:47:46.170 --> 00:47:47.050
Sheryl?

00:48:06.440 --> 00:48:11.990
You see... my departed mother always sang this song to me.

00:48:16.790 --> 00:48:23.380
The mother of my mother, my grandmother, said that it was the fated song of an ancient civilization on some planet.

00:48:24.380 --> 00:48:25.840
From what planet?

00:48:26.800 --> 00:48:28.130
Then do you know why Ranka...

00:48:28.710 --> 00:48:29.630
I don't really know.

00:48:30.630 --> 00:48:32.090
Because it was only the first time,

00:48:33.090 --> 00:48:37.060
in this vast galaxy, that I ever encountered somebody else singing "Aimo."

00:48:37.390 --> 00:48:38.100
How in the...

00:48:39.020 --> 00:48:40.890
Could it be that the incident 11 years ago...

00:48:42.190 --> 00:48:42.850
Incident?

00:48:43.270 --> 00:48:45.480
No, it's nothing.

00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:56.280
I guess it really is a song of fate.

00:48:57.620 --> 00:49:00.660
That girl's singing sounded quite nice.

00:49:03.540 --> 00:49:05.040
It was cute, but...

00:49:05.040 --> 00:49:08.880
it also seemed sad, somewhat lonely.

00:49:09.340 --> 00:49:14.760
I see, it's kind of like how birds sing deep in the forest so that people won't hear them.

00:49:15.510 --> 00:49:17.850
You seem to understand her circumstances quite well.

00:49:18.010 --> 00:49:19.430
I'm a professional after all.

00:49:21.100 --> 00:49:23.730
Also, that girl... Ranka-chan.

00:49:25.190 --> 00:49:28.270
She really loves you.

00:49:28.980 --> 00:49:31.150
Hey, how could you possibly...

00:49:44.120 --> 00:49:45.790
This is Antares 1 calling G.

00:49:46.170 --> 00:49:49.420
The target has left Island 1 and is en route to Island 3,

00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:51.760
with a probable destination of the Zentran Mall.

00:49:52.510 --> 00:49:56.300
Fairy 9 has already landed on Island 3.

00:49:56.890 --> 00:49:58.850
Report any further developments.

00:49:59.100 --> 00:49:59.800
Roger.

00:50:01.180 --> 00:50:04.770
Now, let me witness the power of your song.

00:50:04.810 --> 00:50:07.810
Island 3
Institute of Alien Biology

00:50:08.060 --> 00:50:10.860
We have observed the following from analyzing the Vajra:

00:50:11.190 --> 00:50:14.440
Its carapace is similar in composition to the Valkyrie's energy conversion armor.

00:50:14.990 --> 00:50:16.860
It is capable of producing folds.

00:50:17.070 --> 00:50:20.830
It also produces missile-like objects internally on a continual basis.

00:50:21.790 --> 00:50:23.790
But perhaps the most amazing thing of all...

00:50:24.620 --> 00:50:28.330
is that its control system, its "brain," is very small.

00:50:28.500 --> 00:50:29.290
What?

00:50:29.540 --> 00:50:33.760
In conclusion, we can say that it is issued commands from elsewhere.

00:50:33.760 --> 00:50:35.050
A biological weapon?

00:50:35.970 --> 00:50:40.300
Assuming that these Vajra are being controlled by Galaxy...

00:50:40.470 --> 00:50:43.430
In that case, Sheryl Nome's visit was...

00:50:44.180 --> 00:50:45.600
Galaxy's plot...

00:50:52.940 --> 00:50:54.360
Let's go back after eating.

00:50:54.820 --> 00:50:57.030
The captain is really worried about you.

00:50:57.400 --> 00:51:01.740
No way, Onii-chan has always treated me like a child,

00:51:01.740 --> 00:51:04.370
even though another war could occur at anytime.

00:51:04.870 --> 00:51:07.410
I just want my song to reach out to everyone.

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:14.130
You should stop acting so spoiled, okay?

00:51:16.840 --> 00:51:22.800
You're being selfish. You don't even know how the captain feels when he's fighting. What nerve.

00:51:24.430 --> 00:51:28.850
Though it's true everyone would rather forget the battle from the other day,

00:51:28.850 --> 00:51:30.810
we can't just pretend that nothing happened.

00:51:33.400 --> 00:51:38.280
Anyway, if you believe that you have what it takes to be a singer, Ranka-chan, can you sing right here and now?

00:51:38.280 --> 00:51:41.870
Here in this place where no one came to see you.

00:51:45.330 --> 00:51:47.790
Hey, aren't you done playing around?

00:51:48.040 --> 00:51:49.040
Of course not!

00:51:49.210 --> 00:51:52.580
I told you what I know about "Aimo," so you'd better accompany me until I'm done!

00:52:59.280 --> 00:53:00.400
That voice...

00:53:19.670 --> 00:53:21.800
I give up.

00:53:39.400 --> 00:53:40.730
Deculture!

00:53:41.570 --> 00:53:43.240
Good going, Ranka.

00:53:44.200 --> 00:53:46.030
That child is singing...

00:53:55.370 --> 00:53:57.380
Fold wave confirmed.

00:54:07.050 --> 00:54:07.590
Cathy!

00:54:07.890 --> 00:54:08.300
Hey!

00:54:20.690 --> 00:54:21.570
How...

00:54:25.860 --> 00:54:27.280
That was great.

00:54:27.490 --> 00:54:29.160
Honestly, I was amazed.

00:54:30.830 --> 00:54:32.240
It's all thanks to Alto-kun!

00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:37.580
Speak of the devil...

00:54:40.290 --> 00:54:42.090
Sheryl... -san.

00:54:42.920 --> 00:54:45.510
Thank you, it was really fun.

00:54:48.890 --> 00:54:51.470
That was unexpected; you thanking someone.

00:54:51.680 --> 00:54:56.020
You're annoying, I don't do it often, so be grateful that I did.

00:54:57.230 --> 00:55:01.230
Well then, though I'd like to ask that girl about the "Aimo" thing,

00:55:01.690 --> 00:55:04.110
I have to return for my concert rehearsal.

00:55:05.440 --> 00:55:07.110
Oh yeah, for next week.

00:55:07.360 --> 00:55:09.700
Yep, my "final revenge."

00:55:10.280 --> 00:55:12.990
This time around, I'll be singing even more than last time!

00:55:13.200 --> 00:55:14.540
I guess it can't be helped.

00:55:14.790 --> 00:55:17.620
I'll definitely find your earring and bring it back.

00:55:20.960 --> 00:55:22.540
I'll be waiting, Alto.

00:55:32.720 --> 00:55:33.300
No way.

00:55:33.890 --> 00:55:35.100
You there!

00:55:48.320 --> 00:55:49.070
Ranka!

00:55:51.070 --> 00:55:52.120
Young lady!

00:55:52.120 --> 00:55:55.990
You must be the destined songstress I've been searching for all this time!

00:55:56.370 --> 00:55:58.500
Will you allow me to help you make your debut?

00:55:59.540 --> 00:56:00.500
Debut?

00:56:00.750 --> 00:56:01.370
What?

00:56:01.540 --> 00:56:02.880
Debut you say?

00:56:03.210 --> 00:56:05.630
Your singing shall change the world!

00:56:05.630 --> 00:56:06.750
My singing?

00:56:46.290 --> 00:56:49.550
Long time, no see, Alto-kun. Are you doing well?

00:56:49.840 --> 00:56:53.050
I'm sure S.M.S. training must be really difficult.

00:56:53.640 --> 00:56:57.260
My manager from Vector Productions,
Mr. Elmo, helped me persuade my brother,

00:56:57.260 --> 00:56:59.430
and I finally was able to realize my dream of debuting as a singer!

00:56:59.520 --> 00:57:02.600
Even though I'm starting at small venues, I'll still do my best to sing.

00:57:07.440 --> 00:57:10.940
I recently got to drive a bulldozer for the first time.

00:57:20.370 --> 00:57:22.710
I wonder why I had to wear a swimsuit though.

00:57:50.900 --> 00:57:55.530
Oh! I also went to Deep Akiba dressed as
a Valkyrie to sing promotional campaign songs.

00:57:55.780 --> 00:57:57.320
Obviously, it transformed too!

00:58:16.840 --> 00:58:20.720
Let's go to Nyan-Nyan and eat tuna buns together, okay?

00:58:23.020 --> 00:58:24.230
Together...

00:58:37.990 --> 00:58:40.580
Congratulations on your 25th death.

00:58:41.580 --> 00:58:43.950
You raised the AI difficulty level didn't you?!

00:58:43.950 --> 00:58:46.250
Is it okay to leave things as they are, you two-timing princess?

00:58:46.250 --> 00:58:49.710
The captain won't go easy on you if you make Ranka-chan cry.

00:59:39.800 --> 00:59:42.510
So when exactly will I get to fly a Messiah again?

00:59:42.890 --> 00:59:45.140
Who knows? You'll get to eventually,

00:59:45.140 --> 00:59:47.890
as long as you stop blowing your top.

00:59:48.230 --> 00:59:49.060
What was that?

00:59:49.060 --> 00:59:52.900
There, there, no need to worry. I'm sure you'll get the opportunity to fly right away, Alto-senpai.

00:59:53.270 --> 00:59:56.860
"Right away, right away."
We're not serving take-out at Nyan-Nyan.

00:59:58.190 --> 01:00:00.150
Speaking of Nyan-Nyan...

01:00:00.660 --> 01:00:01.700
Nyan-nyan?

01:00:08.200 --> 01:00:10.410
Really now, lover boy.

01:00:10.540 --> 01:00:11.330
What is it?

01:00:11.670 --> 01:00:13.790
Now's your chance to clear up any misunderstanding...

01:00:14.380 --> 01:00:16.340
from the last time you met.

01:00:18.210 --> 01:00:19.130
Michael.

01:00:28.680 --> 01:00:29.640
Ranka!

01:00:32.020 --> 01:00:36.190
When do you think Ranka-san and Alto-senpai will get back?

01:00:36.690 --> 01:00:37.610
Who knows?

01:00:41.150 --> 01:00:43.490
I'm sorry for not staying in contact with you.

01:00:43.660 --> 01:00:46.780
S.M.S. training was harder than I imagined.

01:00:47.080 --> 01:00:49.500
Oh yeah, I heard from Luca...

01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:52.460
You already made your debut, right? Congratulations!

01:00:52.620 --> 01:00:55.750
I never expected you to be able to convince the stubborn captain–

01:00:55.920 --> 01:00:58.340
your brother that is, to give his permission.

01:00:59.260 --> 01:01:03.550
So... how does it feel to be a singer? I heard that the lessons are tough.

01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:06.010
I hope you aren't pushing yourself too hard.

01:01:07.850 --> 01:01:10.770
What kinds of songs are you singing?

01:01:11.430 --> 01:01:13.940
Next time, let me listen to—

01:01:14.310 --> 01:01:15.190
God damn it!

01:01:16.560 --> 01:01:17.770
Welcome!

01:01:21.030 --> 01:01:21.860
Ranka.

01:01:37.290 --> 01:01:38.290
This song.

01:01:41.880 --> 01:01:44.630
Thank you, this is all possible because of you, Alto-kun.

01:01:45.760 --> 01:01:48.010
It's all because of your words of encouragement.

01:01:48.100 --> 01:01:49.640
Now I can fly too.

01:01:55.020 --> 01:01:58.900
My first commercial jingle starts airing today.

01:02:00.150 --> 01:02:04.360
Though it's limited to Island 1's
Shibuya and San Francisco districts,

01:02:04.360 --> 01:02:07.700
they say it plays in all the shops like this one around Frontier.

01:02:09.160 --> 01:02:10.950
That's wonderful, Ranka!

01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:17.210
Hearing my own singing makes me feel a bit self-conscious though.

01:02:18.330 --> 01:02:21.050
Don't be, you have a nice voice, Ranka.

01:02:27.800 --> 01:02:29.430
About last time, Ranka—

01:02:29.430 --> 01:02:31.560
Hey, Alto-kun.

01:02:32.010 --> 01:02:35.430
What is Sheryl-san to you, Alto-kun?

01:02:45.110 --> 01:02:50.280
She's... Sheryl is... that's right, she's a professional.

01:02:50.370 --> 01:02:51.080
Professional?

01:02:51.410 --> 01:02:52.160
Yeah.

01:02:53.160 --> 01:02:57.920
At first, I thought she was just a good singer with a wild, vile personality.

01:02:58.670 --> 01:03:02.710
However, I never expected her to be really childish and innocent inside.

01:03:03.420 --> 01:03:06.090
At times, she's almost like a totally different person.

01:03:06.720 --> 01:03:11.850
Still, when she's in the spotlight, she's able to bewilder and amaze the audience.

01:03:12.260 --> 01:03:14.640
She's truly a professional singer.

01:03:15.730 --> 01:03:18.270
But aren't you the same, Alto-kun?

01:03:18.350 --> 01:03:20.730
You're said to be the child-star prodigy of the Saotome family.

01:03:22.900 --> 01:03:24.230
That's not the real me.

01:03:25.230 --> 01:03:28.530
I was forced to hone my acting skills ever since I was a child.

01:03:28.570 --> 01:03:30.450
Even though I was small back then,

01:03:30.450 --> 01:03:34.580
I was able please everyone, and they praised me for being pretty.  It was interesting, but still...

01:03:35.700 --> 01:03:40.000
I gradually grew sick of it since it was merely the path my father set for me.

01:03:42.880 --> 01:03:44.300
You seem so distant.

01:03:46.300 --> 01:03:50.010
Even though you're right here beside me, you're so far away.

01:03:51.340 --> 01:03:52.220
Ranka.

01:04:03.060 --> 01:04:05.780
The truth is that I was just scared.

01:04:07.650 --> 01:04:12.070
Before leaving the stage, I played all kinds of roles.

01:04:12.320 --> 01:04:17.750
When you devote your mind and body to a role, you sense this formidable power creeping in.

01:04:20.540 --> 01:04:22.670
You could say that the role itself takes over.

01:04:23.170 --> 01:04:26.050
Am I a man? Am I a woman?

01:04:26.050 --> 01:04:29.510
I couldn't tell who I really was anymore.

01:04:30.420 --> 01:04:34.930
I felt that the existence known as Saotome Alto might completely disappear.

01:04:36.060 --> 01:04:39.770
I got scared, that's why I ran away from the stage.

01:04:47.980 --> 01:04:49.780
You will always be Alto-kun.

01:04:51.780 --> 01:04:53.200
Whatever happens...

01:04:54.120 --> 01:04:55.410
whatever time it may be...

01:04:56.160 --> 01:04:57.950
you will always be Alto-kun.

01:05:00.450 --> 01:05:02.290
Thank you, Ranka.

01:05:13.050 --> 01:05:16.220
Don't get too familiar with this woman, Warrant Officer Alto.

01:05:17.760 --> 01:05:24.100
This woman, Sheryl Nome, visiting here from Galaxy... is suspected of being a spy.

01:05:25.230 --> 01:05:27.730
A spy, you say?! That's absurd!

01:05:27.730 --> 01:05:30.940
Perhaps, but think about it.

01:05:30.940 --> 01:05:33.900
Mere days after Sheryl arrived,

01:05:33.900 --> 01:05:36.570
the Vajra attacked on the day of her concert.

01:05:36.570 --> 01:05:42.960
Also, why would the Galactic Fairy insist on getting close to such a trivial, greenhorn pilot like you?

01:05:43.910 --> 01:05:46.830
That's... because she lost her earrings.

01:05:47.130 --> 01:05:49.340
What if that was the plan all along?

01:05:50.340 --> 01:05:52.210
Then why would she choose someone like me?

01:05:52.630 --> 01:05:54.090
You see...

01:05:54.630 --> 01:05:59.850
Ranka is the lone survivor of a family of Vajra researchers on Gallia 4.

01:06:00.310 --> 01:06:02.980
You happen to be very important to her.

01:06:04.560 --> 01:06:05.440
Ranka?

01:06:09.690 --> 01:06:10.570
That can't be true!

01:06:10.900 --> 01:06:13.320
So that's why she knows about Ranka's song!

01:06:13.440 --> 01:06:14.450
Ranka's song?

01:06:14.950 --> 01:06:19.660
She knows how to sing "Aimo,"
the song that's Ranka's one and only memory.

01:06:19.870 --> 01:06:20.780
What?

01:06:21.660 --> 01:06:22.750
Listen, Alto...

01:06:23.120 --> 01:06:25.920
don't further involve yourself with Sheryl Nome.

01:06:26.460 --> 01:06:30.790
Furthermore, if she dares touch even a single hair on Ranka's head,

01:06:31.050 --> 01:06:32.800
do whatever it takes to stop her.

01:06:36.800 --> 01:06:45.980
195, 196, 197, 198, 199...

01:06:46.350 --> 01:06:50.060
200, 201, 202...

01:06:50.770 --> 01:06:56.650
203, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8...

01:06:57.110 --> 01:06:58.740
What are you mumbling about?

01:06:59.780 --> 01:07:00.700
I was counting the stars.

01:07:02.580 --> 01:07:04.660
I was just about to get to ten thousand too.

01:07:04.660 --> 01:07:06.660
Ten thousand? You counted that many—

01:07:06.960 --> 01:07:08.040
You can see them?

01:07:10.540 --> 01:07:13.050
"A sniper's eye is his life," or so they say.

01:07:13.920 --> 01:07:14.710
Michael.

01:07:15.880 --> 01:07:17.930
So what did you want to talk about?

01:07:22.930 --> 01:07:27.770
Mata Hari, Stephanie von Hohenlohe, Ri Kouran, Sharon Apple.

01:07:28.940 --> 01:07:31.690
They are examples of celebrities who were spies or

01:07:31.690 --> 01:07:35.030
were somehow implicated in terrorist activities.

01:07:35.730 --> 01:07:40.280
It can't be... but... she's... Sheryl is...

01:07:40.360 --> 01:07:42.370
Seriously, you're so naive.

01:07:43.160 --> 01:07:45.580
Are you implying that I was blinded by the face of beauty?

01:07:46.290 --> 01:07:50.460
Giving you that "how could you?" feeling
is something intelligence operatives tend to do.

01:07:53.130 --> 01:07:55.380
You think Sheryl's a spy too, don't you?

01:07:57.090 --> 01:08:00.550
At the very least, the possibility isn't zero.

01:08:02.140 --> 01:08:08.430
Anyway, wouldn't you understand a woman's heart better than I?

01:08:09.020 --> 01:08:13.610
You, who is said to be the prettiest kabuki actor in the galaxy, princess Alto.

01:08:14.360 --> 01:08:15.320
Michael!

01:08:17.820 --> 01:08:20.780
Truly, your talents are wasted on being a pilot.

01:08:24.160 --> 01:08:26.490
Sheryl's Revenge concert starts tomorrow.

01:08:27.660 --> 01:08:31.250
Whatever their scheme, they'll probably begin tonight.

01:09:03.530 --> 01:09:04.870
Astounding area, huh?

01:09:34.980 --> 01:09:37.360
Wow, I've never seen anything like you before.

01:09:37.360 --> 01:09:39.400
Where did you come from?

01:09:41.530 --> 01:09:44.110
You should follow your mama so you don't get lost, okay?

01:09:48.780 --> 01:09:49.910
That tickles!

01:09:51.160 --> 01:09:52.960
Wait, stop it!

01:09:54.830 --> 01:09:56.790
Geez, you're such a child...

01:10:14.480 --> 01:10:16.850
What do I have to do to be more feminine?

01:10:21.900 --> 01:10:23.110
You're so sweet.

01:10:24.150 --> 01:10:28.910
That's right, maybe I can ask Alto to teach me how to dance so I can be more feminine!

01:10:39.750 --> 01:10:40.590
Alto-kun.

01:10:55.230 --> 01:10:56.890
So it was here all along.

01:10:58.270 --> 01:10:59.610
No wonder I couldn't find it.

01:11:00.860 --> 01:11:02.860
Who would call at this late hour?

01:11:05.240 --> 01:11:06.070
Sheryl!

01:11:08.990 --> 01:11:10.570
Hello, this is Saotome.

01:11:11.070 --> 01:11:17.460
I am unable to answer the phone right now. Please leave a message after the beep.

01:11:12.740 --> 01:11:16.210
Geez, I rarely call people like this too...

01:11:18.790 --> 01:11:21.250
Could you... come to Griffith Park?

01:11:21.340 --> 01:11:23.090
Come as soon as you get this.

01:11:23.210 --> 01:11:26.420
I won't let you off easy if you don't show!

01:11:29.890 --> 01:11:31.140
What's this all about?

01:11:54.580 --> 01:11:55.870
It took you long en—

01:11:58.040 --> 01:11:59.580
Sheryl-san?

01:12:00.620 --> 01:12:03.460
What are doing out this late, Ranka-chan?

01:12:05.800 --> 01:12:09.340
I'll be starting my first mini-concert soon.

01:12:10.220 --> 01:12:12.890
Congratulations! So you're finally getting your real debut!

01:12:13.430 --> 01:12:18.930
No, it's nothing compared to yours. It's just a small street concert.

01:12:19.020 --> 01:12:20.850
I just feel a bit nervous.

01:12:21.270 --> 01:12:24.520
The more I thought about it, the harder it was to sleep.

01:12:24.610 --> 01:12:29.490
So I thought maybe I could ask Alto-kun to teach me how to dance, but I couldn't bring myself to ask.

01:12:29.950 --> 01:12:32.660
What am I rambling on for?

01:12:35.910 --> 01:12:37.370
Aren't you cute?

01:12:39.120 --> 01:12:40.250
But I...

01:12:41.080 --> 01:12:45.250
Don't worry about it. Alto and I were just playing around.

01:12:45.880 --> 01:12:46.630
Playing around?

01:12:52.050 --> 01:12:53.800
Please come with Alto.

01:12:55.300 --> 01:12:56.350
These are...

01:12:59.770 --> 01:13:03.440
Sheryl Nome will forever be the Galactic Fairy.

01:13:03.940 --> 01:13:07.110
Sometimes I wish I could return to who I once was.

01:13:58.240 --> 01:13:58.870
What?

01:13:59.990 --> 01:14:01.620
You... it can't be...

01:14:02.410 --> 01:14:03.540
Why?

01:14:06.750 --> 01:14:08.710
What's happening to you, Ai-kun?

01:14:08.790 --> 01:14:09.540
Ai-kun?

01:14:10.550 --> 01:14:14.550
Yeah, I found him earlier today, so I took him in.

01:14:15.930 --> 01:14:17.510
That's amazing in any case.

01:14:18.100 --> 01:14:21.680
It definitely reacted to your singing.

01:14:21.930 --> 01:14:23.060
To my singing?

01:14:23.560 --> 01:14:26.310
You came from that planet, right?

01:14:26.520 --> 01:14:28.520
That planet, Gallia 4.

01:14:29.310 --> 01:14:30.820
Gallia 4?

01:14:31.070 --> 01:14:32.780
That's right, don't you remember?

01:14:33.530 --> 01:14:35.820
I was born and raised on that planet as well.

01:14:36.360 --> 01:14:39.280
I have no memories of my childhood.

01:14:40.620 --> 01:14:41.450
No memories?

01:14:43.910 --> 01:14:45.290
I'm very sorry.

01:14:59.010 --> 01:14:59.760
Ai-kun!

01:15:03.970 --> 01:15:04.980
Ai-kun!

01:15:06.180 --> 01:15:08.810
Wait! Wait, I said!

01:15:09.980 --> 01:15:10.770
Sheryl?

01:15:14.440 --> 01:15:15.110
Ranka?

01:15:16.360 --> 01:15:17.280
Wait!

01:15:19.110 --> 01:15:19.950
Ranka!

01:15:20.870 --> 01:15:21.870
Stop it!

01:15:22.490 --> 01:15:23.240
Alto?

01:15:23.290 --> 01:15:24.790
Get your hands off Ranka!

01:15:30.790 --> 01:15:33.340
Why? Why would you do this to Ranka?

01:15:33.840 --> 01:15:35.460
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

01:15:36.010 --> 01:15:36.760
Don't move!

01:15:37.920 --> 01:15:42.050
I never wanted to believe it; that you're a spy for Galaxy.

01:15:42.430 --> 01:15:44.640
Spy? Why would I...

01:15:45.390 --> 01:15:48.980
You're here to eliminate Ranka, a survivor of Gallia 4.

01:15:49.480 --> 01:15:52.560
You only got close to me for the sake of your search for Ranka!

01:15:53.480 --> 01:15:55.030
You're wrong, Alto-kun.

01:15:55.030 --> 01:15:58.360
Sheryl was just following me because I was trying to catch Ai-kun, who was running away.

01:15:59.070 --> 01:15:59.910
Ai-kun?

01:16:06.330 --> 01:16:10.830
You're terrible, I was wrong about you, Alto.

01:16:14.380 --> 01:16:15.170
Hey!

01:16:15.550 --> 01:16:16.550
Sheryl-san.

01:16:28.560 --> 01:16:32.190
There's no doubt about it, Colonel Grace.

01:16:33.230 --> 01:16:37.860
We've finally found what we've been looking for, "Code Q1."

01:16:39.280 --> 01:16:44.070
However, isn't the fold wave pattern from her singing still a bit weak?

01:16:44.530 --> 01:16:48.040
I'm actually more interested in that green creature.

01:16:48.040 --> 01:16:50.710
There is no corresponding data regarding it in our libraries.

01:16:51.290 --> 01:16:53.750
Perhaps it's a larval Vajra, don't you think?

01:16:54.000 --> 01:16:56.800
Still, we should hasten our activities.

01:16:57.000 --> 01:16:59.340
There isn't much time left.

01:17:00.090 --> 01:17:02.510
What about the mission arrangements for tomorrow?

01:17:02.510 --> 01:17:06.220
Fairy 9 seems to be emotionally distressed.

01:17:06.640 --> 01:17:08.100
Please do not worry.

01:17:08.680 --> 01:17:16.060
I give you my word that "Fairy 9," Sheryl Nome, won't only be happy, but also angry and sad.

01:17:16.060 --> 01:17:18.440
She'll have everything that gives power to her singing.

01:17:19.280 --> 01:17:25.410
And I'm sure that the dormant power in that
other girl's singing, "Code Q1," will finally awaken.

01:17:25.490 --> 01:17:28.030
Such admirable confidence.

01:17:28.080 --> 01:17:32.960
Certain people have already become suspicious of you while you've been hanging around.

01:17:33.120 --> 01:17:34.620
Aren't you concerned?

01:17:34.670 --> 01:17:38.090
By the time they it figure out, that child will already be working for our benefit

01:17:38.130 --> 01:17:39.800
and to my heart's content.

01:17:39.840 --> 01:17:40.710
Roger.

01:18:05.700 --> 01:18:08.490
Leave the investigation regarding Galaxy to us.

01:18:08.700 --> 01:18:11.120
I'm placing you under house arrest for a day.

01:18:11.120 --> 01:18:11.750
But...

01:18:12.160 --> 01:18:13.500
Shut up, kid!

01:18:16.580 --> 01:18:19.090
Even if she isn't here to attack Ranka,

01:18:19.250 --> 01:18:22.630
she is without a doubt connected to "Aimo" and Gallia 4.

01:18:23.470 --> 01:18:26.050
Don't approach her until we're able sort things out.

01:18:26.340 --> 01:18:28.720
But tomorrow is Sheryl's final—

01:18:28.720 --> 01:18:30.810
What is more important, singing or human lives?

01:18:31.510 --> 01:18:32.520
No way...

01:18:48.160 --> 01:18:55.410
Sheryl Nome: Final Revenge Live will be starting in 2 hours.
Please be patient.

01:18:56.250 --> 01:19:00.540
Sheryl Nome:  Final Revenge Live, starting in 2 hours.

01:19:06.130 --> 01:19:09.470
Captain, the point inspection for each section is underway,

01:19:09.680 --> 01:19:11.810
and the outfitting of the ship has been completed.

01:19:13.430 --> 01:19:15.100
It's seems we're going to be busy.

01:19:15.980 --> 01:19:20.360
I sense that there might be some kind of major movement tonight.

01:19:20.940 --> 01:19:24.570
Tonight? Does it have something to do with Sheryl's final concert?

01:19:24.820 --> 01:19:28.450
An all out Vajra attack won't be a mere a skirmish.

01:19:29.030 --> 01:19:32.660
When it finally occurs, it'll definitely be a heated life and death struggle.

01:19:33.120 --> 01:19:35.330
Is that your intuition as a sailor?

01:19:37.330 --> 01:19:43.750
The wounds of the past tend to itch whenever a storm is imminent.

01:19:44.460 --> 01:19:45.510
Captain.

01:19:50.220 --> 01:19:51.140
Your excellency...

01:19:51.720 --> 01:19:52.470
What is it?

01:19:52.720 --> 01:19:53.760
It's an SOS.

01:20:23.080 --> 01:20:25.380
<i>I was wrong about you, Alto.</i>

01:20:26.760 --> 01:20:27.840
Sheryl.

01:20:30.880 --> 01:20:33.220
A gem that can convey...

01:20:35.100 --> 01:20:36.720
her feelings.

01:20:59.160 --> 01:21:00.160
What the...

01:21:08.670 --> 01:21:09.550
Sheryl?

01:21:17.890 --> 01:21:19.520
No...

01:21:20.430 --> 01:21:22.350
Alone...

01:21:23.440 --> 01:21:26.860
Don't leave me all alone.

01:21:28.570 --> 01:21:29.940
All alone...

01:21:35.990 --> 01:21:38.410
Don't leave me all alone?!

01:21:40.750 --> 01:21:41.700
Sheryl!

01:21:50.210 --> 01:21:51.970
Down, down...

01:21:52.800 --> 01:21:54.050
All right, stop!

01:21:55.590 --> 01:22:00.060
Check the positions of the lights from L1 to L72!

01:22:08.310 --> 01:22:09.190
Alto!

01:22:10.230 --> 01:22:10.900
Sheryl.

01:22:11.320 --> 01:22:13.780
Please listen to me. I'm very sorry about the other day—

01:22:13.780 --> 01:22:14.400
Go away!

01:22:18.910 --> 01:22:19.700
Sheryl.

01:22:20.200 --> 01:22:23.080
At least let me return this to you.

01:22:24.000 --> 01:22:25.210
That's...

01:22:33.800 --> 01:22:35.970
You may never forgive me,

01:22:35.970 --> 01:22:40.260
and I don't know if you're really a spy or not,

01:22:41.640 --> 01:22:43.680
but let me at least tell you this one thing.

01:22:44.730 --> 01:22:46.480
No matter what happens,

01:22:46.480 --> 01:22:49.440
you aren't alone!

01:22:55.280 --> 01:22:56.740
What are you talking about all of the sudden?

01:22:57.910 --> 01:23:05.540
I believe that these, your earrings, conveyed
the feelings that were buried deep inside your heart.

01:23:08.290 --> 01:23:10.040
How egotistical of you.

01:23:10.750 --> 01:23:13.000
There's no reason for me to feel alone.

01:23:13.460 --> 01:23:14.340
Sheryl.

01:23:18.970 --> 01:23:20.930
That was a wonderful conclusion.

01:23:21.220 --> 01:23:23.470
Now, it's about time.

01:23:23.470 --> 01:23:24.100
What?

01:23:24.640 --> 01:23:28.810
The audience shouldn't conceal themselves. Come out.

01:23:29.400 --> 01:23:30.150
Audience?

01:23:32.400 --> 01:23:38.030
So you knew all along? As expected of Galaxy's cyborg.

01:23:38.070 --> 01:23:38.660
Captain!

01:23:39.660 --> 01:23:40.950
You tricked me!

01:23:41.030 --> 01:23:42.450
No! I...

01:23:43.330 --> 01:23:44.870
Grace O'Connor.

01:23:44.990 --> 01:23:47.960
No, Colonel Grace Godunuwa.

01:23:48.460 --> 01:23:54.590
Under the Galaxy Security Treaty, Article 17, you are hereby detained under suspicion of being a spy.

01:23:55.130 --> 01:23:57.130
What an outrageous tale.

01:23:57.170 --> 01:23:57.720
What?

01:23:58.170 --> 01:24:00.470
Listen to this closely, Sheryl.

01:24:01.340 --> 01:24:04.560
It's almost as though they were
waiting for your concert to end first.

01:24:06.720 --> 01:24:11.940
Two hours ago, or to be more precise, at 21:13, Galactic Standard Time,

01:24:12.190 --> 01:24:18.400
I received word that our mother fleet, Galaxy, came under attack by the Vajra.

01:24:19.070 --> 01:24:19.950
Galaxy is...

01:24:22.160 --> 01:24:23.370
Mayday, mayday.

01:24:24.030 --> 01:24:26.410
Our forces on the mainland are almost wiped out.

01:24:26.410 --> 01:24:27.620
Please, anyone, send—

01:24:30.210 --> 01:24:33.670
Galaxy sent an SOS signal to Frontier.

01:24:34.290 --> 01:24:38.130
However, your government decided to pretend that they never heard it.

01:24:38.380 --> 01:24:39.050
You're lying...

01:24:39.550 --> 01:24:43.260
My father... the government wouldn't do such a terrible thing.

01:24:45.010 --> 01:24:47.310
Rumors are flying around at Galaxy...

01:24:47.930 --> 01:24:50.690
that Frontier discovered the true nature of the Vajra,

01:24:50.690 --> 01:24:53.480
and are planning to monopolize them as their own resource.

01:24:53.560 --> 01:24:54.730
What's that?!

01:24:55.320 --> 01:24:56.400
Is this true?!

01:24:56.900 --> 01:25:01.990
It's true, it made me see Frontier as an even more terrible place.

01:25:02.030 --> 01:25:03.030
No way.

01:25:04.910 --> 01:25:07.490
Army superiors have received classified information...

01:25:08.200 --> 01:25:13.290
that Galaxy's SOS signal is nothing but sabotage and will be ignored.

01:25:13.580 --> 01:25:14.420
How stupid!

01:25:15.250 --> 01:25:16.960
You understand it now, don't you?

01:25:16.960 --> 01:25:21.920
For the sake of achieving it's own agenda,
Frontier willingly violated galactic treaties,

01:25:21.920 --> 01:25:23.630
and abandoned its own compatriots.

01:25:23.630 --> 01:25:24.890
How could...

01:25:25.260 --> 01:25:28.310
What are Galaxy's losses so far, Grace?

01:25:28.430 --> 01:25:31.230
One-third of the frigates have already been destroyed.

01:25:31.230 --> 01:25:33.640
The fall of the mainland is only a matter of time.

01:25:34.020 --> 01:25:35.690
Why have you kept quiet about this?

01:25:35.690 --> 01:25:40.820
I had no choice. There's nothing we could do anyway, with Galaxy so far away.

01:25:40.820 --> 01:25:45.200
I mean, we're not the New U.N. Spacy or a private army.

01:25:48.450 --> 01:25:51.290
How much will it cost to hire the S.M.S. for a combat mission?

01:25:51.370 --> 01:25:51.950
What?

01:25:52.250 --> 01:25:53.210
Answer me!

01:25:53.290 --> 01:25:57.420
Is Galaxy telling the truth?
Is the Frontier government telling the truth?

01:25:57.420 --> 01:25:59.130
Don't you want to know who's right?

01:25:59.800 --> 01:26:01.090
Interesting.

01:26:01.550 --> 01:26:04.510
The Galactic Fairy wants to become a Goddess of Battle?

01:26:04.840 --> 01:26:07.010
Don't do it, Ozma! It might be a trap!

01:26:07.390 --> 01:26:09.640
One hundred and twenty million credits.

01:26:10.520 --> 01:26:13.980
That will account for the use of all standard weaponry and the Macross Quarter.

01:26:14.600 --> 01:26:17.150
The use of optional weaponry is charged separately.

01:26:18.440 --> 01:26:19.480
That's a good price.

01:26:22.030 --> 01:26:23.570
Here's a Vega Black Card.

01:26:23.990 --> 01:26:27.370
If that's not enough, I'll give you the royalties from my next album.

01:26:27.700 --> 01:26:30.240
Well, we'll be gambling our lives on this.

01:26:30.910 --> 01:26:31.830
Lives...

01:26:35.670 --> 01:26:39.170
What, aren't you a pro too? Do you have a problem with this?

01:26:39.750 --> 01:26:43.170
No, I joined S.M.S. to protect those in need.

01:26:44.010 --> 01:26:47.720
I just never expected you to spend your own money on it.

01:26:50.930 --> 01:26:53.220
Return it to me after the mission is over.

01:26:54.930 --> 01:26:56.730
Intact, of course.

01:26:57.480 --> 01:26:58.520
Sheryl.

01:26:59.150 --> 01:27:02.860
The deal is sealed! Our captain has authorized it.

01:27:03.110 --> 01:27:06.400
Are you serious?
This is why I don't support military privatization.

01:27:06.950 --> 01:27:10.990
Warrant Officer Alto, we and the rest of S.M.S.

01:27:10.990 --> 01:27:15.120
shall immediately commence the Galaxy fleet rescue mission.

01:27:15.910 --> 01:27:18.920
Codename: "Galactic Fairy."

01:27:29.180 --> 01:27:30.890
No abnormalities detected on the hull.

01:27:31.050 --> 01:27:32.560
Defold successful.

01:27:33.560 --> 01:27:37.560
We have confirmation of Galaxy Fleet refugees directly ahead, bearing 022.

01:27:38.100 --> 01:27:39.230
Zooming on image.

01:27:41.940 --> 01:27:42.770
How horrible.

01:27:43.110 --> 01:27:47.280
The enemy Vajra seem to have a battlecruiser-class ship.

01:27:48.320 --> 01:27:51.370
Determine the enemy force's location and composition, Monica.

01:27:51.370 --> 01:27:51.870
Roger.

01:27:51.990 --> 01:27:54.040
Open all channels, Ram.

01:27:54.240 --> 01:27:57.000
Inform the refugee ships that we will be providing assistance from here on.

01:27:57.000 --> 01:27:57.660
Roger.

01:27:57.750 --> 01:28:01.380
Order all Destroid units to prepare for anti-aircraft combat, Mina.

01:28:01.670 --> 01:28:02.790
Roger.

01:28:03.460 --> 01:28:04.460
Cathy.

01:28:04.550 --> 01:28:05.510
Yes!

01:28:05.550 --> 01:28:10.050
Our tactics here at S.M.S. are a bit more aggressive than the army's.

01:28:10.180 --> 01:28:12.010
You'd better prepare yourself.

01:28:12.850 --> 01:28:14.390
Just bring it on!

01:28:15.970 --> 01:28:17.770
All hands to battle stations!

01:28:28.950 --> 01:28:30.660
Listen to my song!

01:29:16.870 --> 01:29:17.450
Incoming!

01:29:17.740 --> 01:29:20.120
All units, Totsugeki Love Heart!

01:29:25.670 --> 01:29:26.790
Let's go, Michael.

01:29:27.210 --> 01:29:30.920
Formation MM Genus, make sure you don't miss!

01:29:32.050 --> 01:29:33.430
You don't have to tell me that.

01:29:45.310 --> 01:29:47.020
Keep focused, here they come!

01:29:47.190 --> 01:29:47.610
Yes, sir!

01:30:09.000 --> 01:30:10.000
It's started.

01:30:18.510 --> 01:30:20.970
As if I'd fall behind!

01:30:37.910 --> 01:30:38.870
Fire!

01:30:49.840 --> 01:30:51.840
All right! Three ships destroyed!

01:30:58.180 --> 01:30:59.430
Take this!

01:31:16.450 --> 01:31:20.280
The refugee ships are about to reach the fold safety zone.

01:31:48.560 --> 01:31:49.230
What?!

01:31:54.820 --> 01:31:56.440
Three refugee ships have been destroyed.

01:31:56.940 --> 01:31:57.740
No survivors...

01:31:58.450 --> 01:31:59.240
That's...

01:31:59.320 --> 01:32:00.070
No way.

01:32:02.370 --> 01:32:03.530
How could this happen?

01:32:08.410 --> 01:32:12.000
M5 and 6, M5 and—

01:32:14.170 --> 01:32:15.000
Alto-kun?

01:32:20.220 --> 01:32:21.050
But why...

01:32:24.760 --> 01:32:25.600
Onii-chan?!

01:32:29.190 --> 01:32:32.560
It's me, I wanted to tell you in person,

01:32:33.150 --> 01:32:34.820
but it's kinda hard to explain.

01:32:35.480 --> 01:32:37.530
I have work. I won't be back tonight.

01:32:38.110 --> 01:32:38.780
Work?

01:32:41.410 --> 01:32:43.320
However, I promise that I'll be back soon, along with everyone else.

01:32:43.530 --> 01:32:45.080
Don't worry about it while you're waiting.

01:32:47.500 --> 01:32:48.330
No way...

01:32:50.210 --> 01:32:51.830
Then Alto-kun is also...

01:32:56.880 --> 01:32:58.510
Is that their mothership?

01:32:59.380 --> 01:33:00.380
Skull 4!

01:33:01.380 --> 01:33:02.970
Get out of there, Alto!

01:33:06.220 --> 01:33:08.520
I know, but...

01:33:10.480 --> 01:33:12.560
we can't let them do any more damage.

01:33:27.160 --> 01:33:29.120
If we can just destroy this one...

01:33:48.260 --> 01:33:51.430
This next song is very precious to me.

01:33:52.390 --> 01:33:57.820
I think everyone here will keep living life with many new encounters and farewells.

01:33:58.190 --> 01:34:01.650
But the feeling of not wanting to lose something important...

01:34:05.240 --> 01:34:06.410
Sheryl-san.

01:34:13.290 --> 01:34:17.290
Will all of you allow me to speak a little more?

01:34:18.460 --> 01:34:21.670
I want to dedicate this precious song to a certain someone.

01:34:22.050 --> 01:34:25.130
No... to a certain group of people.

01:34:25.890 --> 01:34:29.850
To the people who are far away, putting their lives on the line for everyone's sake.

01:34:31.560 --> 01:34:35.940
She knows... She knows about it.

01:34:36.560 --> 01:34:38.310
But she still...

01:35:35.830 --> 01:35:37.580
This is... singing?

01:35:47.930 --> 01:35:49.090
This light...

01:35:50.890 --> 01:35:53.220
The Vajra forces have stopped firing.

01:35:53.760 --> 01:35:55.270
They're preparing to fold!

01:35:55.770 --> 01:35:56.350
Fold?!

01:35:56.430 --> 01:35:59.940
Could they be chasing after the Galaxy refugee ships?

01:36:08.950 --> 01:36:10.820
All hands, emergency fold.

01:36:11.320 --> 01:36:14.200
Withdraw all units and prepare to pursue the Vajra!

01:36:29.630 --> 01:36:30.380
Defold?

01:36:39.730 --> 01:36:41.770
This is... Frontier?!

01:36:58.750 --> 01:36:59.370
No way!

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:02.000
Why would they appear at an important time like this?

01:37:03.500 --> 01:37:05.790
Alto-kun... Onii-chan...

01:37:06.840 --> 01:37:11.470
They've arrived as expected, guided by those girls' fold songs.

01:37:12.630 --> 01:37:14.600
What should we do? At this rate we'll—

01:37:29.780 --> 01:37:32.200
Don't tell me the Vajra are headed <i>here</i>?

01:37:37.740 --> 01:37:40.660
That's... Sheryl's live concert venue!

01:37:42.040 --> 01:37:44.790
Battle Frontier, charge state: 85%.

01:37:45.380 --> 01:37:48.170
All friendly forces within the firing trajectory, withdraw as soon as possible.

01:37:48.750 --> 01:37:51.470
Collecting energy for the Macross Cannon.

01:37:51.630 --> 01:37:55.340
90, 91, 92, 93...

01:37:56.220 --> 01:37:58.970
The enemy battleship has entered our main gun's line of fire.

01:37:59.220 --> 01:38:02.230
Set the large enemy warship as the target.

01:38:02.350 --> 01:38:04.190
Main gun, locked on target.

01:38:04.480 --> 01:38:06.230
All hands, prepare to fire!

01:38:08.360 --> 01:38:09.860
Main gun, fire!

01:38:21.580 --> 01:38:22.750
Direct hit on the target!

01:38:28.090 --> 01:38:30.380
Wait... the target remains!

01:38:30.630 --> 01:38:31.210
What the—

01:38:31.210 --> 01:38:31.960
Impossible!

01:38:41.180 --> 01:38:43.140
It's the Vajra again, why?

01:38:51.150 --> 01:38:51.980
<i>It's the Vajra.</i>

01:38:52.070 --> 01:38:53.650
<i>Run away, Ranka!</i>

01:38:54.650 --> 01:38:57.660
<i>I think that you are the Vajra's target.</i>

01:38:58.700 --> 01:38:59.950
<i>Me?</i>

01:39:02.540 --> 01:39:04.660
The Vajra want... me?

01:39:13.920 --> 01:39:20.970
At this rate... At this rate, we're all going to die.

01:39:23.560 --> 01:39:25.270
Hurry up and take cover, Sheryl!

01:39:26.020 --> 01:39:27.440
But I'm not done yet!

01:39:37.360 --> 01:39:38.160
Sheryl!

01:39:39.490 --> 01:39:41.410
Over here! We need to escape quickly!

01:39:42.030 --> 01:39:44.290
Why are you here, Alto?

01:39:44.490 --> 01:39:46.080
What about the refugees from Galaxy?

01:39:46.160 --> 01:39:47.920
They're fine, hurry, get on!

01:39:53.670 --> 01:39:54.500
Alto-kun?!

01:39:55.710 --> 01:39:56.420
The Vajra!

01:39:56.760 --> 01:39:59.680
At this rate, everyone's... Alto's going to...

01:40:06.770 --> 01:40:07.810
At this rate...

01:40:26.660 --> 01:40:30.670
What if... What if the Vajra really <i>are </i>after me.

01:40:34.710 --> 01:40:38.340
I... I...

01:40:53.690 --> 01:40:54.520
Ranka!

01:40:57.230 --> 01:40:57.900
What the...?

01:41:00.610 --> 01:41:04.120
Is she... using herself as bait for the Vajra?

01:41:04.240 --> 01:41:08.160
Ranka-chan is using herself as bait, Alto.

01:41:08.200 --> 01:41:08.750
Really?

01:41:09.000 --> 01:41:10.330
Go! Hurry!

01:41:10.410 --> 01:41:11.290
Damn it!

01:41:24.220 --> 01:41:25.510
Alto-kun...

01:41:29.980 --> 01:41:30.640
Ranka!

01:41:36.150 --> 01:41:37.900
What do the Vajra want with Ranka?

01:41:48.870 --> 01:41:49.910
Alto!

01:42:06.260 --> 01:42:10.930
I can still... I can still sing... even if there are Vajra!

01:42:36.580 --> 01:42:37.500
Sheryl?

01:42:54.310 --> 01:42:56.900
Her fold wave has risen to level 9?

01:42:57.650 --> 01:43:01.860
Could it be that the "Code Q1" powers, a power lying dormant inside "Fairy," has finally awoken?

01:43:03.240 --> 01:43:05.900
What are you all doing? Broadcast Sheryl's performance!

01:43:06.610 --> 01:43:08.240
But who would want to—

01:43:08.780 --> 01:43:13.160
Sheryl is risking her life singing on stage in order to give us courage!

01:43:14.290 --> 01:43:16.040
Hurry up and broadcast it to the whole ship!

01:43:16.670 --> 01:43:19.790
We need to tell everyone that there's still hope!

01:43:20.170 --> 01:43:21.000
Hope?

01:43:21.210 --> 01:43:22.090
Hope!

01:43:22.380 --> 01:43:23.090
Okay!

01:43:23.800 --> 01:43:25.340
Start up all the remote cameras!

01:43:25.470 --> 01:43:28.300
We're gonna broadcast Sheryl's singing to the entire ship!

01:43:32.140 --> 01:43:33.060
Grace!

01:43:54.950 --> 01:43:56.500
Sheryl... she's...

01:44:03.630 --> 01:44:04.710
Sheryl...

01:44:17.980 --> 01:44:21.350
Block B17's artificial gravity control system has been damaged!

01:44:25.110 --> 01:44:26.030
Ranka!

01:44:32.200 --> 01:44:33.620
Ranka!

01:44:34.370 --> 01:44:35.160
Alto-kun?!

01:44:38.290 --> 01:44:39.160
Sheryl-san?

01:44:40.620 --> 01:44:42.080
Sheryl-san is still singing!

01:44:59.810 --> 01:45:01.020
This time I'll...

01:45:06.980 --> 01:45:09.570
This is Antares 1 to S.M.S. pilot,

01:45:09.950 --> 01:45:11.570
I'll be providing assistance.

01:45:11.700 --> 01:45:12.360
Assistance?

01:45:12.740 --> 01:45:13.820
Antares 1, you say?

01:45:15.370 --> 01:45:18.790
Do you copy? Then hurry up! Chase after that Vajra.

01:45:19.620 --> 01:45:20.330
Roger!

01:45:38.140 --> 01:45:42.600
Leave the defense of this place to us, Sheryl. You should sing as much as you like!

01:45:43.560 --> 01:45:46.230
Okay! You don't have to tell me!

01:46:15.470 --> 01:46:17.970
This is bad, is that thing trying to run away?

01:46:21.850 --> 01:46:22.770
It's the city.

01:46:30.440 --> 01:46:31.030
Ranka.

01:46:36.240 --> 01:46:38.620
No you don't!

01:47:13.570 --> 01:47:14.780
Ranka!

01:47:15.360 --> 01:47:16.200
Alto-kun!

01:47:38.510 --> 01:47:39.390
Ranka!

01:47:39.640 --> 01:47:40.600
Alto-kun!

01:47:47.190 --> 01:47:47.890
It's too far away!

01:47:52.440 --> 01:47:53.150
That's too risky!

01:47:58.700 --> 01:47:59.530
Get down!

01:48:14.130 --> 01:48:14.800
Ranka!

01:48:15.210 --> 01:48:16.130
Alto-kun!

01:48:18.800 --> 01:48:19.680
Ranka!

01:48:22.550 --> 01:48:23.470
This is bad!

01:48:25.680 --> 01:48:26.980
Go, Alto!

01:48:27.600 --> 01:48:28.140
Michael!

01:48:33.940 --> 01:48:34.770
Michael!

01:48:39.490 --> 01:48:40.280
Ranka!

01:48:43.700 --> 01:48:44.410
Alto-kun.

01:49:06.680 --> 01:49:07.390
Sheryl.

01:49:07.560 --> 01:49:09.180
Alto, Ranka-chan?!

01:49:12.480 --> 01:49:13.440
Sheryl-san!

01:49:13.770 --> 01:49:15.190
Let's go, Ranka-chan!

01:49:15.770 --> 01:49:16.440
Sure!

01:50:07.490 --> 01:50:10.200
Concentrate the pinpoint barrier on the tip of our gun!

01:50:19.500 --> 01:50:20.460
Hit it with everything we've got!

01:50:35.600 --> 01:50:37.980
The enemy warship's fold barrier has vanished!

01:50:38.980 --> 01:50:40.730
Now's our chance! Fire the Macross Cannon!

01:51:13.640 --> 01:51:16.190
The Vajra army has begun retreating via fold.

01:51:20.730 --> 01:51:22.320
We've...

01:51:25.650 --> 01:51:26.780
Won?

01:51:28.910 --> 01:51:32.580
Of course! This is how the S.M.S. fights!

01:51:36.750 --> 01:51:40.040
However, we still suffered heavy losses.

01:51:42.300 --> 01:51:47.220
Inform all sections that we will be commencing relief and rescue operations.

01:51:47.380 --> 01:51:48.090
Roger!

01:52:00.520 --> 01:52:03.610
Michael! Michael!

01:52:06.360 --> 01:52:07.070
Michael...

01:52:20.170 --> 01:52:22.420
Yo, you sure are late, Klan!

01:52:23.210 --> 01:52:24.130
Michael.

01:52:25.920 --> 01:52:26.840
Michael!

01:52:35.640 --> 01:52:38.230
So this is the power of the songstresses...

01:52:56.620 --> 01:53:01.830
This is S.M.S. Skull Squadron member,
Warrant Officer Saotome Alto, to Antares 1.

01:53:02.540 --> 01:53:04.590
I am grateful for your assistance.

01:53:06.090 --> 01:53:08.090
I merely did what I had to do.

01:53:12.010 --> 01:53:13.140
It's snowing!

01:53:22.400 --> 01:53:23.600
How beautiful.

01:53:26.230 --> 01:53:27.780
The snow of mourning.

01:53:30.030 --> 01:53:31.200
Onii-chan!

01:53:33.820 --> 01:53:35.200
Are you all right, Ranka?

01:53:36.370 --> 01:53:38.620
Geez, I'm not a kid anymore.

01:53:40.330 --> 01:53:42.460
You did a wonderful job, Ranka.

01:53:43.040 --> 01:53:44.080
Alto-kun.

01:53:51.470 --> 01:53:52.430
Sheryl.

01:53:53.510 --> 01:53:54.390
Ranka.

01:53:55.510 --> 01:53:57.430
You both sang very well.

01:53:58.510 --> 01:53:59.520
Alto.

01:54:02.270 --> 01:54:07.270
We managed to rescue seven of the refugee ships from Galaxy. As for the other three...

01:54:08.320 --> 01:54:09.110
I'm sorry.

01:54:15.200 --> 01:54:17.530
I know you did your best.

01:54:18.490 --> 01:54:20.120
I can ask for nothing more.

01:54:21.290 --> 01:54:24.870
You can keep it, consider it a bonus for protecting all of us.

01:54:26.380 --> 01:54:28.630
But this is your precious—

01:54:29.050 --> 01:54:32.220
I told you you've earned it. Be grateful and take it.

01:54:32.550 --> 01:54:35.260
This isn't a service I often bestow.

01:54:44.020 --> 01:54:47.110
Thank you Alto, Ranka-chan.

01:54:49.940 --> 01:54:53.650
Now I know that I'm not alone.

01:54:58.830 --> 01:54:59.990
Sheryl-san.

01:55:02.120 --> 01:55:04.160
I'm not alone, huh?

01:59:16.080 --> 01:59:18.920
Macross F The Movie
-Wings of Goodbye-
